- Rewrote the generation route/control tests (13 files + 1 new schema test) to prove the actual ADR-0030 behaviors instead of journal replay: resubmitting a candidate returns the existing generation, activating the already-active generation with the current epoch is a no-op, and a stale epoch still rejects — plus a fresh-schema test proving `generation_control_journal` no longer exists.

`pnpm verify` passes: typecheck, format, lint, and the full suite (94 files / 639 tests) all green. Committed as `119a7ceee709b00c0dd3883582f835e93c801e64` (conventional commit, pre-commit gate ran clean). Wrote the report to `/Users/aditya/repos/projects/cf-stumble/.audit/v0/tasks/T2.md` with per-criterion evidence and an explicit list of what was deliberately left untouched (generation/decisions/startup-check internals, `feature-map.md`, `slices.md` — all outside T2's listed scope).

